   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT making an appropriation to pay to the children of the late David F.\nGantt, member of the Assembly from the 137th Assembly District, the balance\ndue of his unpaid annual compensation for a portion of the year 2020",
    "basePrintNo": "S7187",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7187-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Appropriations",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7187\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act making  an appropriation to pay to the children of the late David\nF. Gantt, member of the Assembly from the 137th Assembly District, the\nbalance due of his unpaid annual compensation for a portion of the year\n2020\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize payment of unpaid annual compensation to Kathleen A.  Hope,\nTroy C. Hightower and Troy E. Sizer, children of David F.  Gantt, member\nof the Assembly from the 137th Assembly District.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one authorizes the sum of fifty thousand seven hundred sixty-\nnine dollars and twenty-two cents ($50, 769.22) to be appropriated out\nof the general fund for payment to Kathleen A. Hope, Troy C. Hightower\nand Troy E. Sizer, the children of the late David F. Gantt, who died on\nthe first day of July, 2020, for the balance due of the unpaid annual\ncompensation which would have been earned by him had he continued to\nlive and serve as such member of the assembly until the end of 2020.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIt has been the tradition of the Legislature to pay the unpaid salary of\nan Assemblymember who dies in office to the widow/widower or other fami-\nly member of such member.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\n$50,769.22.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
